;; Classic multi-shot hazard: a continuation is captured inside a function
;; call (f), which then RETURNS normally, and only afterward is the saved
;; continuation invoked again from a completely different dynamic extent
;; (top level, after several intervening calls to display/newline).
;;
;; This is the shape escape-only setjmp/longjmp continuations cannot handle:
;; by the time of the second invocation, f's native stack frame has been
;; popped and its memory reused by the intervening calls.
;;
;; MEASURED BEHAVIOR (2026-08-25, .icc/silent-wrong-ledger.yaml SW-51):
;;   native JIT (-r): CRASHES — SIGILL ("illegal instruction"), after
;;                    printing "f returned: 2" and
;;                    "about to re-invoke k after f's extent exited".
;;                    Eshkol's own signal handler catches it and reports
;;                    "this is most likely a stack overflow" (a reasonable
;;                    guess given the symptom, but the actual cause is
;;                    longjmp restoring a stack/frame-pointer state whose
;;                    backing memory has been overwritten).
;;   native AOT:      Same SIGILL, same point.
;;   bytecode VM:     Does NOT crash — correctly prints
;;                    "re-invoke result: 11" and then "done". The VM
;;                    captures continuations by snapshotting its own
;;                    operand stack and call-frame array (not the C stack),
;;                    so re-entering a popped Scheme-level frame is not
;;                    inherently unsafe there the way it is for setjmp/
;;                    longjmp. (Contrast with generator_coroutine.esk, where
;;                    a second re-entry on the VM DOES go wrong — the VM's
;;                    continuation support is not fully multi-shot either,
;;                    it is just broken in a different way than native's.)
;;
;; This fixture is deliberately NOT wired into any pass/fail CI harness
;; (native crashes by design here). Run manually, e.g.:
;;   ./build/eshkol-run -r tests/continuations/reentry_after_function_return.esk
(define k #f)
(define (f)
  (+ 1 (call/cc (lambda (c) (set! k c) 1))))
(display "f returned: ") (display (f)) (newline)
;; f has now returned. Invoke the saved continuation from a completely
;; different dynamic extent (top level, after several intervening calls).
(display "about to re-invoke k after f's extent exited") (newline)
(if k
    (let ((k2 k))
      (set! k #f)
      (display "re-invoke result: ")
      (display (k2 10))
      (newline)))
(display "done") (newline)
